# Section 2: Building Blocks of Scalability

## 1. Overview

This section covers the fundamental patterns used to build scalable, available, and resilient systems:

- Vertical scaling
- Horizontal scaling
- Load balancing
- Load-balancing algorithms
- Stateless services
- Service discovery
- Circuit breakers
- Timeouts
- Retries
- Fallbacks
- Graceful degradation

> Scalability is not simply adding more servers. A scalable system must allow servers to be added, removed, replaced, discovered, routed to, and protected without breaking the user experience.

